# TOOLS.md — your tools & credentials reference (example)

Copy this to `TOOLS.md` and fill it in with **your** tools. It's injected into the
owner's sessions (see `CLAUDE.md` → "This Session"), so the assistant knows which
CLIs it can call and where credentials live.

> **Never put secret values in this file.** Keep secrets in `.env` or a gitignored
> `secrets/` dir and only *reference* them here. `TOOLS.md` itself can stay private
> too if you'd rather not commit your tool list.

## Secrets convention

- All credentials live in `secrets/*.env` (gitignored) or the bot's `.env`.
- This file *names* a tool and *points at* its secret — it never contains the secret.

## Example tools (replace with your own)

- **gh** — GitHub CLI. `gh pr list`, `gh run list`. Auth via `gh auth login`.
- **&lt;email-cli&gt;** — read/triage the inbox. Creds: `secrets/email.env`.
  e.g. `mail search "in:inbox is:unread"`
- **&lt;calendar-cli&gt;** — list/create events. Creds: `secrets/calendar.env`.
- **&lt;music-api&gt;** — now-playing / listening stats. Creds: `secrets/music.env`.
- **curl · node · python3 · git · ffmpeg** — general-purpose, no creds.

## Telegram targets

- Chat id: `<your supergroup id>` (also in `.env` as `CHAT_ID`).
- Topic id → name mapping lives in `src/config.ts` (`TOPICS`) — keep that the source of truth.

## Notes / gotchas

- Document anything future-you will forget: rate limits, token TTLs, odd flags.
- If a service needs periodic re-auth, write down **how** here — so a 3 a.m. session
  isn't stuck guessing.
